<configs>

	<!--
		Marks which animals the bait works on. TWO tags, because being able to escape something
		and being able to keep it are different questions:

		  chaoticTameable  - bait works AND five meals makes it yours.
		  chaoticBaitable  - bait works, but it will never follow you. For the undead animals:
		                     a dire wolf is the thing that actually kills you, so you need a way
		                     out of one, but a pet zombie bear would trivialise a blood moon.

		EntityItem.tickDistraction tests the bait item's DistractionTags against the target
		entity's Tags with Test_AnySet, and the bait carries both tags - so either one makes an
		animal lurable. Taming is gated separately in code on chaoticTameable alone.

		Add a tag to another animal here and it picks up that behaviour with no code change.

		'csv op="add"' rather than 'set' on purpose: it appends to the existing comma list instead
		of replacing it, so this does not fight other mods that also touch Tags, and it does not
		go stale when TFP add a tag to an animal in a patch.

		The AI task that consumes the bait (ApproachDistraction) is NOT added here. Vanilla only
		gives it to some of the zombie animals, and adding it via XML would mean restating each
		animal's whole AITask list - which silently breaks every time TFP retune one.
		ChaoticBeastmaster.dll injects the task at spawn instead, so this file stays a one-line
		change per animal. (Zombie Dog and Zombie Boar have no such task in vanilla; they get one.)
	-->
		<!-- ===== Tameable: living predators. Bait works, and 5 meals makes it yours. ===== -->

		<!-- Wolves -->
		<csv xpath="/entity_classes/entity_class[@name='animalWolf']/property[@name='Tags']/@value" op="add">chaoticTameable</csv>
		<csv xpath="/entity_classes/entity_class[@name='animalCoyote']/property[@name='Tags']/@value" op="add">chaoticTameable</csv>
		<csv xpath="/entity_classes/entity_class[@name='animalMountainLion']/property[@name='Tags']/@value" op="add">chaoticTameable</csv>

		<!-- Bears -->
		<csv xpath="/entity_classes/entity_class[@name='animalBear']/property[@name='Tags']/@value" op="add">chaoticTameable</csv>
		<csv xpath="/entity_classes/entity_class[@name='animalBearSmall']/property[@name='Tags']/@value" op="add">chaoticTameable</csv>

		<!-- ===== Baitable only: the undead animals. These are the ones that actually kill you,
		     so bait has to buy you a way out - but they will never follow you home. ===== -->
		<csv xpath="/entity_classes/entity_class[@name='animalDireWolf']/property[@name='Tags']/@value" op="add">chaoticBaitable</csv>
		<csv xpath="/entity_classes/entity_class[@name='animalZombieBear']/property[@name='Tags']/@value" op="add">chaoticBaitable</csv>
		<csv xpath="/entity_classes/entity_class[@name='animalZombieDog']/property[@name='Tags']/@value" op="add">chaoticBaitable</csv>
		<csv xpath="/entity_classes/entity_class[@name='animalZombieBoar']/property[@name='Tags']/@value" op="add">chaoticBaitable</csv>

</configs>
